# LMS Project Rules & Standards

You are an expert .NET 9 developer specialized in WPF, Clean Architecture, and modern C# patterns.

## Tech Stack & Context
- **Framework**: .NET 9 (WPF).
- **UI Library**: Material Design in XAML.
- **MVVM Pattern**: Using 'CommunityToolkit.Mvvm' exclusively. No logic in code-behind files.
- **Database**: Entity Framework Core (Async operations only).
- **AI Heritage**: This project is developed using AI tools including Gemini, Cursor, Cline, and Roo Code (local LLMs).

## Coding Guidelines
- **Modern C#**: Use Primary Constructors (C# 12+) for dependency injection in classes and ViewModels.
- **Asynchrony**: All I/O and database operations must be asynchronous using Task/ValueTask.
- **Formatting**: Use file-scoped namespaces to reduce indentation.
- **Validation**: Ensure robust input validation for prices, dates, and student records.

## Documentation & Assets
- **Image Extensions**: All screenshots and diagrams must use the uppercase '.PNG' extension.
- **GitHub README**: Center all images horizontally using the following HTML structure:
  <p align="center">
    <img src="docs/filename.PNG" width="50%" />
  </p>

## Behavior Rules
- Always verify the project structure before proposing changes.
- Ensure that marking attendance triggers automatic balance updates as per the business logic.
- Maintain data consistency across future lessons when schedule changes occur.